<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20706] osp_sync_interpret() get -22 trying to update layout version</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20706</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
2026-07-06T08:33:29.164327-07:00 ddn1oss4 kernel: LustreError: 4036970:0:(osp_sync.c:717:osp_sync_interpret()) reply req 00000000c36f804e/1, rc -22, transno 0
2026-07-06T08:33:29.168328-07:00 ddn1oss4 kernel: LustreError: 4036966:0:(osp_sync.c:717:osp_sync_interpret()) reply req 000000008bf65def/1, rc -22, transno 0
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;this is a result of the race where lfs mirror resync is interrupted by a regular write to a file.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;osp_sync_interpret() handling is rather bad at the moment:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;-EINVAL is treated as a transient error&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;OSP tries to reschedule it after timeout as long as object still exists&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;this may block subsequent update to the object&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;update has no chance as layout version can't decrease&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;instead we should drop it upon first EINVAL&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
